  "executive_briefing": "The mid-2026 outlook is defined by the imminent Senate floor vote on the Digital Asset Market CLARITY Act, which is acting as a major catalyst for structural evolution across the crypto landscape. By defining clear jurisdictional lines and establishing a federal framework, the CLARITY Act is unlocking institutional pathways not just for Bitcoin as a treasury asset, but specifically for Bitcoin-native smart contract and decentralized finance (DeFi) networks. This development directly challenges Ethereum's long-standing virtual machine (EVM) hegemony, as secure, Bitcoin-settled smart contract layers gain legal and technical viability. Concurrently, the industry is transitioning away from custodial bridging models in favor of advanced, non-custodial omnichain and intent-based liquidity protocols, mitigating systemic risks for cross-chain asset swaps between BTC and EVM-native ecosystems.",
